# Understanding the nexus skill

The **nexus** is the runtime that backs `server` units, agents, data, sync, and the
compile/weave lane — one nexus serves many sites. Understanding it explains where
server-side code runs, how a workbook is hosted, and why one nexus is the org. This
skill is the conceptual + operational reference for the nexus.

When the user asks where server code runs, how hosting works, or how the nexus scales,
load the references below.

app :understanding_the_nexus do
  title       "Understanding the nexus"
  description "Understand the nexus runtime: what it is, how it runs server units and serves many sites, and how to run one. Use when reasoning about where server-side code runs or how a workbook is hosted."

  section "Concept" do
    page "introduction/what-is-the-nexus"
    page "blog/the-nexus-serves-many-sites"
  end

  section "Operating it" do
    page "deploy/running-the-nexus"
  end
end
